When iterating over properties of CMS objects (e.g. with @cms.page.each@) the resolved values of
reference properties (like "folder", "creator", ...) will no longer be CMS objects but their string
representation instead.
The old behaviour could easily lead to endless loops when doing something like @println(cms.page)@ or
transforming CMS objects to their JSON representation.
See "Accessing cms":https://www.gentics.com/Content.Node/cmp8/guides/groovy.html#accessing-cms in the
guides for details.
